 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "Yaskawa iQpump Micro drives using the built-in RS-485/422 MEMOBUS/Modbus terminals, per user manual TOEP YAIQPM 03B.",
 "summary": "Yaskawa's compact pump drive with built-in pump functions and an RS-485/422 MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU port. Command registers (run bits, frequency reference, PID target, outputs) start at 0001H, status and monitor registers at 0020H, and parameters are reachable at their hex numbers. This map covers the command and status words, key monitors, fault/alarm bits and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 31,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "Register numbers are hex and sent unchanged: the manual's read example asks slave 2 for starting register 0020H as Starting No. 00H 20H. Parameters use the hex numbers in the parameter list (H5-01 = 0425H)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive iQpump Micro User Manual",
  "doc_number": "TOEP YAIQPM 03B",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TOEPYAIQPM03&cmd=documents&documentName=TOEPYAIQPM03.pdf",
  "pages": "Appendix C: H5 setup parameters pp. 391-393, function codes p. 397, read example p. 399, C.10 MEMOBUS/Modbus data table pp. 401-405 (command data p. 401, monitor data pp. 403-405), C.11 Enter command p. 415; parameter list hex numbers (b1 p. 320, H5 pp. 343-344)."
 },
 "notes": [
  "Frequency registers 0002H, 0023H and 0024H use the units chosen in o1-03, so they are left unscaled.",
  "Left out: 0007H analog output and 000AH pulse output settings, 0025H output voltage (unit switched by H5-10), 0026H output current (unit given by a footnote that varies), 0027H output power, 0028H/0032H torque, 002FH frequency reference bias, 003EH/003FH output frequency in r/min or 0.01 % (sign not stated), the U-monitor blocks from 0040H and the real-time-clock registers 3004H-3030H.",
  "Only function codes 03H (read, max. 16 registers), 08H (loopback) and 10H (write multiple) are supported; use 10H for single writes.",
  "The manual disagrees on the H5-01 range: section C.5 and the slave-address text give 0-20H, the parameter list gives 0-FFH. H5-02 accepts 0-5 (up to 38400 bps) per C.5 even though the speed table prints settings up to 8.",
  "With H5-11 = 0 (default), parameter writes take effect only after the Enter command (0900H or 0910H). Command registers do not need Enter.",
  "Data length 8 bits and 1 stop bit are fixed."
 ],
